+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U3","attempt":5,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/ui/U3/verdicts/A4-reviewer.json R1; docs/trace/ui/U3/verdicts/A4-security.json S1 (round A4, head 61c63e9)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"LOOP-4","layer":"api","files":["src/web/compiler/plans.ts","tests/web/unit/compiler/loop-4.test.ts"],"root_cause":"This is reviewer R1 (P1). The layer is the ui compiler; it is recorded as 'api' because the layer enum has no ui value, the same as in A2 and A3. Symptom: on U3's own round A3 (docs/trace/ui/U3/findings/A3.md:13), I1's Cause field stops at a quoted '\"Symptom:\"', and the rest of the cause shows under Symptom. I2's Fix direction field opens on a stray quote, and the quoted marker words are lost. Cause: at 61c63e9 the marker pattern in splitRootCause (src/web/compiler/plans.ts:237, packet docs/trace/ui/U3/packet/diff.patch:35025) has no position or quote condition, so every 'Symptom:', 'Cause:' or 'Fix direction:' anywhere in the text becomes a split point, including one that a sentence quotes. That breaks the function's own contract at :232, 'Every character lands in a field', and the A3/I1 fix direction. The tests could not see it. loop-4.test.ts:170 MARKER_NAME and :174 wordsOf strip every marker name wherever it appears before comparing words, so a quoted marker that was dropped or moved still passes expectEveryWord (:193). Every fixture text put markers only at the start of a sentence. Rule: LOOP-4 shows symptom, cause and fix direction as recorded, and DATA-2's 'recorded' means verbatim. Fix direction: a marker counts as a split point only where it opens the text or a sentence and is not inside a quotation. A quoted marker stays as words in the field around it. The word check in the tests must strip only the real split markers. Already done: the red commit 55e5364 adds four tests (loop-4.test.ts:305-346), including U3's real A3 text. Their check, expectEveryWordAsWritten (:297), strips nothing. gate.red